      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sylvania was founded in 1833 by Judge William Wilson and General David White, just 30 years after Ohio became a state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofsylvania.com/visitors/sylvania/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from Latin sylvan, meaning “forest land,” reflecting the dense woods that once covered the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvania%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1858, Sylvania built its own depot on the Erie-Kalamazoo Railroad, and the original station building now stands in the Historical Village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvania%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sylvania hosts the Sylvania Historical Village, an open‑air museum that includes the original 1800s log home and the depot that operated for over a century.",
